{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-109881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}0.5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0.5\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-0.45 \\\\ 1.55\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-109881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is a stochastic vector. Indeed, \n\n- its entries are all nonnegative, and\n\n- the entries add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.5+0+0.5=1\n$$\n\n- Vector $v$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $w$ is *not* a stochastic vector since the entries do not add up to one:\n\n$$\n0+0=0\\ne 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$u$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-109881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-109881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-109881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$u$ and $v$ only"] ["text" "$u$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$u$ only"] ["text" "$u$, $v$, and $w$"] ["text" "$v$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-109881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$u$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}-0.2 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.5\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}0.6 \\\\ -0.1 \\\\ 0.5\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0.15 \\\\ 0.95\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $v$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $w$is *not* a stochastic vector since the entries do not add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.15+0.95=1.1\\ne 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-135485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$u$ and $v$ only"] ["text" "$u$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$u,$ $v,$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$w$ only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}0.45 \\\\ 0.55 \\\\ -0.05\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}0.7 \\\\ 0.3\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0.65 \\\\ 0.15 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $v$ is a stochastic vector. Indeed, \n\n- its entries are all nonnegative, and\n\n- the entries add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.7+0.3=1\n$$\n\n- Vector $w$ is a stochastic vector. Indeed, \n\n- its entries are all nonnegative, and\n\n- the entries add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.65+0.15+0.2=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$v$ and $w$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-135483" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135483" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$u$ and $v$ only"] ["text" "$u,$ $v,$ and $w$"] ["text" "$v$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$v$ only"] ["text" "$w$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135483" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ and $w$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are stochastic vectors?\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}0.15 \\\\ 0.85\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 \\\\ -0.1 \\\\ 0.3\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 0.3 \\\\ 0.5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our vectors in turn.\n\n- Vector $u$ is a stochastic vector. Indeed, \n\n- its entries are all nonnegative, and\n\n- the entries add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.15+0.85=1\n$$\n\n- Vector $v$ is *not* a stochastic vector since it contains negative entries.\n\n- Vector $w$ is a stochastic vector. Indeed, \n\n- its entries are all nonnegative, and\n\n- the entries add up to one:\n\n$$\n0.2+0.3+0.5=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$u$ and $w$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-135484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$u$ and $v$ only"] ["text" "$u$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$u$ only"] ["text" "$u,$ $v,$ and $w$"] ["text" "$w$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$u$ and $w$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are stochastic matrices?\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0 & 0.9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0.9 & 0 & 0.1\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a stochastic vector is a vector with nonnegative entries that add up to $1.$ A matrix is stochastic if all its columns are stochastic vectors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices in turn.\n\n- Matrix $U$ is *not* a stochastic matrix since its second column is not a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries don't add up to one): \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0 & 0.9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0.9 & 0 & 0.1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Matrix $V$  is *not* a stochastic matrix since its first column is not a stochastic vector (it contains negative entries): \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 1.1 & 0.8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Matrix $W$ is a stochastic matrix. Indeed, each column is a stochastic vector (the corresponding entries are non-negative and add up to one): \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0.5 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.7\\end{aligned}]\\,\\begin{aligned}0.5+0.5=1 \\\\ 0.3+0.7=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$W$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-135488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$U$ and $V$ only"] ["text" "$U$ and $W$ only"] ["text" "$U$ only"] ["text" "$V$ and $W$ only"] ["text" "$W$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$W$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "There are three cable TV providers in a particular apartment block: provider $A,$ provider $B,$ and provider $C.$ A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C,$\n\n- from the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & a & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & b \\\\ c & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the tenants using provider $A,$ $80%$ swap to provider $B$ and $10%$ swap to provider $C.$  This implies that $10%$ of them continue using provider $A.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $B,$ $25%$ swap to provider $A$ and $25%$ swap to provider $C.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue using provider $B.$\n\n- From the tenants using provider $C,$ $70%$ swap to provider $A$ and $10%$ swap to provider $B.$ This implies that $20%$ of them continue using provider $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Provider A** | **Provider B** | **Provider C** |\n| To: | **Provider A** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.7$ |\n| **Provider B** | $0.8$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ |  |\n| **Provider C** | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |  |\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.25 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.5 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.25 & 0.2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.1+0.1=0.45.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-135566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.45"] ["math" "0.55"] ["math" "0.7"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "1.25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.45"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A study shows that in a particular region\n\n- there is a $62%$ chance of another rainy day after a rainy day, and\n\n- there is a $55%$ chance of another dry day after a dry day.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how the weather changes?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the following situation for each day: \n\n- If it is rainy today, there is a $62%$ chance it will be rainy tomorrow. This implies that if it is rainy today, there is a $38%$ chance that it will be dry tomorrow.\n\n- If it is dry today, there is a $55%$ chance that it will be dry tomorrow. This implies that if it is dry today, there is a $45%$ chance that it will be rainy tomorrow\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.62 & 0.45 \\\\ 0.38 & 0.55\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-135556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.38$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.62$ | $0.55$ |  |"] ["text" "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.45$ | $0.38$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.55$ | $0.62$ |  |"] ["text" "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.45$ | $0.62$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.55$ | $0.38$ |  |"] ["text" "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |"] ["text" "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.55$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.45$ |  |"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A study shows that for a particular area in a specific season,\n\n- on a day that follows a day without precipitation, there is a $25%$ chance to have rain and a $35%$ chance to have snow.\n\n- on a day that follows a rainy day, there is a $40%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have snow.\n\n- on a day that follows a snowy day, there is a $50%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have rain.\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.25 & b & 0.05 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.05 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the following situation for this area:\n\n- On a day that follows a day without precipitation, there is a $25%$ chance to have rain and a $35%$ chance to have snow. This implies a $40%$ chance of not having precipitation on this day.\n\n- On a day that follows a rainy day, there is a $40%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have snow. This implies a $55%$ chance of having rain on this day.\n\n- On a day that follows a snowy day, there is a $50%$ chance not to have precipitation and a $5%$ chance to have rain. This implies a $45%$ chance of having snow on this day.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **No Precipitation** | **Rain** | **Snow** |\n| To: | **No Precipitation** | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n| **Rain** | $0.25$ | $0.55$ | $0.05$ |  |\n| **Snow** | $0.35$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ |  |\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.25 & 0.55 & 0.05 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.05 & 0.45\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.4+0.55+0.45=1.4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-135565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.6"] ["math" "0.75"] ["math" "0.8"] ["math" "0.95"] ["math" "1.4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135565" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-35843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a particular country, there are two groups of people: those who are healthy and those who are sick. A study has shown that each quarter\n\n- $38%$ of the healthy people tend to get sick, and\n\n- $45%$ of the sick people tend to improve their health.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how people's health status changes?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-35843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the following situation for each semester: \n\n- $38%$ of the healthy people tend to get sick. This implies that $62%$ of them remain healthy.\n\n- $45%$ of the sick people tend to improve their health. This implies that $55%$ of them remain sick.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Healthy** | **Sick** |\n| To: | **Healthy** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Sick** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.62 & 0.45 \\\\ 0.38 & 0.55\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-35843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Co