e_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "There are two groups of children in a certain city: those who prefer ice cream and those who prefer cakes. A study has shown that, each week\n\n- from the children that prefer ice cream, $35%$ change to cakes, and\n\n- from the children that prefer cakes, $42%$ change to ice cream.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how these children change their preferences each week?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the following situation for each week: \n\n- $35%$ of children who preferred ice creams swap to cakes. This implies that $65%$ of them continue to prefer ice creams.\n\n- $42%$ of children who preferred cakes swap to ice creams. This implies that $58%$ of them continue to prefer cakes.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Ice-creams** | **Cakes** |\n| To: | **Ice-creams** | $0.65$ | $0.42$ |\n| **Cakes** | $0.35$ | $0.58$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.65 & 0.42 \\\\ 0.35 & 0.58\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cour