essful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.8\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0.3 \\\\ 0.7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the state vector ${x}_{1},$ we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.3 \\\\ 0.7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.17 \\\\ 0.83\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-135447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.17 \\\\ 0.83\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.21 \\\\ 0.79\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.23 \\\\ 0.77\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.27 \\\\ 0.73\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.32 \\\\ 0.68\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0.17 \\\\ 0.83\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-35789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-35789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the state vector ${x}_{2},$ we apply two steps of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0},\\,{x}_{2}=P{x}_{1}\n$$\n\nAfter the first step, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, after the second step, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =P{x}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.484 \\\\ 0.516\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-35789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f350f2f30415b1235ad1687b3058d"} {"question" "q-35789" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-35789" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.39 \\\\ 0.61\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.484 \\\\ 0.516\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.516 \\\\ 0.484\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0.844 \\\\ 0.156\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-35789" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0.484 \\\\ 0.516\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.2 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.6 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & 0.4\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.5 \\\\ 0.4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the state vector ${x}_{1},$ we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.2 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.6 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.2 & 0.4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.5 \\\\ 0.4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.29 \\\\ 0.43 \\\\ 0.28\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/state.json" "file_sha256" "79004fa3fa51cf2a2777d0ed4ba28f70a7776f2ba9a7a98f4f8794d869078062"} {"question" "q-135442" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059948/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7ef70fe7b4b12a5ec69f5ea1dc190f1f351f35